# repv-test-servers.csv.example - the two servers tests/integration.sh drives.
#
#     cp repv-test-servers.csv.example .repv-test-servers.csv
#     $EDITOR .repv-test-servers.csv
#
# Or leave this file alone and point CDB_TEST_SERVERS somewhere else.
#
# READ THIS FIRST. The integration suite CREATES AND DELETES DATABASES on both
# of these servers. Every database it makes is prefixed zz_test_ and teardown
# only ever removes that prefix, but a bug in the code under test is exactly
# what the suite exists to find. Point it at two CouchDB instances you would be
# happy to destroy and rebuild - a pair of containers, a pair of scratch VMs -
# and never at anything holding data you would miss.
#
# There is no default. The suite refuses to start until this file exists, so
# there is no way to run it accidentally against whatever happens to be nearby.
#
# Exactly two aliases, named exactly this:
#
#   test0   the source: the suite writes documents here and replicates them out
#   test1   the target: mirrors and snapshots land here, and get pruned here
#
# They must be two different servers - the suite replicates between them.
#
# The format is the tool's own servers table (see repv-servers.csv.example), and
# it is read by the same parser: no credentials in the url, scheme://host[:port]
# with no path. The suite pins itself to plain http, because it writes these
# urls back out into the throwaway servers tables it generates and matches log
# lines on them.
#
alias,url

test0,http://192.168.66.30:5984
test1,http://192.168.66.31:5984
